==Dutch==
{{wikipedia|dab=Aalst|lang=nl}}

===Etymology===
* (''Buren'') First attested as ''aelst'' around 1400. Etymology uncertain. A proposed derivation from {{m|nl|els|t=alder, ''Alnus''}} with collectivising suffix ''-t'' does not match well with old attestations of the toponym. Potentially derived from {{inh|nl|gem-pro|*alhust|t=dwelling place, shrine}}. Compare {{m|nl|Elst}}, {{m|nl|Maasniel}} and {{m|nl|Nieuwaal}}.

